    "q-213389": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213389",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $28,$ the additive inverse of $7$ modulo $28$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $7$ modulo $28$ is the integer $0\\le x<28$ such that\n\n$$\nx+7≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,28).\n$$\n\nNotice that $-7+7≡0,$ so $x≡-7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,28).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-7 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,28) \\\\  & ≡0-7 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,28) \\\\  & ≡28-7 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,28) \\\\  & ≡21 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,28)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $7$ modulo $28$ is $21.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n7+21≡28≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,28)\n$$\n\n**Note:** The additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
