    "q-213385": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213385",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $35,$ the additive inverse of $23$ modulo $35$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $23$ modulo $35$ is the integer $0\\le x<35$ such that\n\n$$\nx+23≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,35).\n$$\n\nNotice that $-23+23≡0,$ so $x≡-23\\,(\\text{mod}\\,35).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-23 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,35) \\\\  & ≡0-23 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,35) \\\\  & ≡35-23 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,35) \\\\  & ≡12 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,35)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $23$ modulo $35$ is $12.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n12+23≡35≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,35)\n$$\n\n**Note:** The additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
