    "q-213387": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213387",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $38,$ the additive inverse of $16$ modulo $38$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $16$ modulo $38$ is the integer $0\\le x<38$ such that\n\n$$\nx+16≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,38).\n$$\n\nNotice that $-16+16≡0,$ so $x≡-16\\,(\\text{mod}\\,38).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-16 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,38) \\\\  & ≡0-16 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,38) \\\\  & ≡38-16 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,38) \\\\  & ≡22 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,38)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $16$ modulo $38$ is $22.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n22+16≡38≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,38)\n$$\n\n**Note:** The additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
