    "q-213382": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213382",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $22,$ the additive inverse of $14$ modulo $22$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $14$ modulo $22$ is the integer $0\\le x<22$ such that\n\n$$\nx+14≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,22).\n$$\n\nNotice that $-14+14≡0,$ so $x≡-14\\,(\\text{mod}\\,22).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-14 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,22) \\\\  & ≡0-14 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,22) \\\\  & ≡22-14 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,22) \\\\  & ≡8 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,22)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $14$ modulo $22$ is $8.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n8+14≡22≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,22)\n$$\n\n**Note:** The additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
