    "q-213336": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213336",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $17,$ the additive inverse of $34$ modulo $17$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $34$ modulo $17$ is the integer $0\\le x<17$ such that\n\n$$\nx+34≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,17).\n$$\n\nFirst, note that $34≡2\\cdot 17≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,17),$ and $0+0≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,17).$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $34$ modulo $17$ is $0.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n34+0≡2\\cdot 17+0≡2\\cdot 0+0≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,17)\n$$\n\n**Note:** In general, the additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
