    "q-213345": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213345",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $8,$ the additive inverse of $19$ modulo $8$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $19$ modulo $8$ is the integer $0\\le x<8$ such that\n\n$$\nx+19≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).\n$$\n\nFirst, we note that $19≡3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}19 & ≡2\\cdot 8+3 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡2\\cdot 0+3 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡3 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, note that $-3+3≡0,$ so $x≡-3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-3 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡0-3 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡8-3 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡5 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $19$ modulo $8$ is $5.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}19+5≡24≡3\\cdot 8≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** In general, the additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
